# card elementwise-operations (user 2026-11-02): a `.op` of plain values is the plain operator, a scalar is the one-element case

# every element-wise operator on two numbers
'3 .* 3'	9
'6 ./ 2'	3
'3 .+ 4'	7
'5 .- 2'	3
'2 .^ 3'	8
'7 .% 4'	3
'3 .< 4'	1
'3 .== 3'	1
'x = 3; x .* x'	9
'square(x) := x .* x; square(3)'	9
'x = 2.5; x .* 2'	5

# any plain value, not only numbers
'"a" .+ "b"'	"ab"

# mixed: a number beside a list maps over the list
'3 .* [1, 2]'	[3 6]
